👋 Introduction
So what exactly are React Hooks?
Let’s break it down in simple terms — with real-world examples.
🧠 What Are Hooks?
State (useState)
Lifecycle (useEffect)
Context (useContext)
Refs (useRef)
Memoization (useMemo, useCallback)
They work only in functional components and eliminate the need for class-based components in most cases.
✅ Why Hooks?
Benefits:
Less boilerplate
Easier to read and reuse
No this keyword mess
🔁 Commonly Used Hooks
import { useState } from 'react';

function Counter() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>
      Clicked {count} times
    </button>
  );
}

